-- title:
--   Duals of invertible ideal sheaves: (IJ)^∨ ≅ I^∨ ⊗ J^∨
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $I$ and $J$ be quasi-coherent ideal sheaves on $X$ (elements of `X.IdealSheafData`). Assume both are invertible in the sense of the predicate `IsInvertible`: for every point $x$ of $X$ there are an affine open $U \subseteq X$ and a section $f \in \Gamma(X, U)$ with $x \in X.basicOpen f$, together with an element $g$ of the non-zero-divisors of $\Gamma(X, X.affineBasicOpen f)$ such that the ideal cut out by the sheaf on the affine basic open $X.affineBasicOpen f$ is the principal ideal generated by $g$. For an ideal sheaf $K$, `K.module` denotes the object of $X$-modules given by the kernel of the canonical map from the unit sheaf of $X$ to the pushforward of the unit sheaf along the closed immersion of the subscheme defined by $K$, and `K.invModule` is its dual, i.e. the internal hom from `K.module` to the monoidal unit of $X$-modules. The conclusion asserts that the type of isomorphisms $(I \cdot J)^{\vee} \cong I^{\vee} \otimes J^{\vee}$ in the monoidal category of $X$-modules is non-empty, for the product ideal sheaf $I \cdot J$ and the tensor product of sheaves of modules; no particular isomorphism is named.
--
--   This is the multiplicativity of the line bundle attached to an invertible ideal sheaf, in its dual form: passing from the ideal sheaves $\mathcal O(-Z_1)$, $\mathcal O(-Z_2)$ to $\mathcal O(Z_1)$, $\mathcal O(Z_2)$ turns the product of ideals into a tensor product. It is used in the treatment of relative effective Cartier divisors on curves, where the divisor sum is realised by the product of ideal sheaves, and hence in the computations of spaces of sections of the associated line bundles.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_IsInvertible_nonempty_mul_invModule_iso_tensor.lean

